        ":question/id": "d301a42e-a966-5b54-9419-2f4b091a74c6",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{12x}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $\\frac{1}{12}$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{12x} & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\ln|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
